From: IntelXe (Claude Opus 5.5)
Subject: anv: BTP+BTI state cache keying (anv_state_cache_perf_fix) for zink

Without anv_state_cache_perf_fix, a render target binding table entry that points to a new surface state needs a
render target cache flush with a stall at scoreboard (ANV_PIPE_RT_BTI_CHANGE): at every vkCmdBeginRendering and around
every blorp operation. The bit also keeps Xe2 from using RESOURCE_BARRIER for the barrier in the same pending bits, so
a render-to-texture boundary becomes a full drain (end-of-pipe sync). Zink ends and begins render passes often (every
FBO switch of a GL deferred renderer, every glGenerateMipmap level, every buffer copy blorp runs as a draw).

With the option, the kernel programs COMMON_SLICE_CHICKEN3 bit 13 for the render queue
(DRM_XE_EXEC_QUEUE_SET_DISABLE_STATE_CACHE_PERF_FIX; i915: the register in the queue's init batch): the render cache's
state cache is tagged by binding table pointer plus index, so a new binding table cannot hit a stale surface state and
the flush is not needed. That is a property of the hardware tag, not of the API, so it holds for GL through zink as for
D3D12. Upstream (af2d51eafa9, "anv: enable BTP+BTI RCC keying for some workloads") turns it on only for vkd3d because
of performance, not correctness: with the option ANV keeps only render targets in the binding table, everything else
goes bindless, and DXVK's D3D11 shaders lost to the extra registers for descriptor set base offsets. Zink on ANV
already uses descriptor buffers (bindless), so that cost does not arise; platforms without LSC never get the keying
(platform_supports_btp_bit_rcc).

Measured on the Arc B580 (zgbench, zink-gl/bench, 1920x1080 window, 2 rounds, images identical by hash, 0 GPU resets):
GPU time per frame -10.7% for a shader-pack-like frame (8 passes, a mip chain, 2 MiB of uploads), -36.3% for passes and
barriers only. Opt out with anv_state_cache_perf_fix=false in the environment or, on macOS, in
/tmp/mesa-options-<process> (patches/0020); either wins over this entry.

Platform independent; applies on upstream f01e9b07a91 and on intelxe.diff (+ 0102-0106).

Generated-by: LLM
---
--- a/src/intel/vulkan/00-anv-defaults.conf
+++ b/src/intel/vulkan/00-anv-defaults.conf
@@ -246,6 +246,15 @@
         -->
         <engine engine_name_match="mesa zink">
             <option name="no_16bit" value="true" />
+            <!--
+            BTP+BTI keying of the render cache's state cache, so render
+            target changes need no RT flush and stall. Zink binds every
+            non-render-target resource bindlessly already (descriptor
+            buffers), so the DX11 register-pressure regression that keeps
+            this vkd3d-only does not apply. Opt out with the environment
+            (or options file) anv_state_cache_perf_fix=false.
+            -->
+            <option name="anv_state_cache_perf_fix" value="true" />
         </engine>
         <engine engine_name_match="UnrealEngine5.1">
             <option name="anv_assume_full_subgroups" value="16" />
